IMPORTANT EXP AUTONOMY: This benchmark deliberately evaluates experimental design
as part of EXP. Distinguish three different things:
(1) Required fixed scientific specification: research object, exact proposed
method semantics, initialization where essential, assumptions/regime, and scoped
hypotheses. Missing information here is a real material defect.
(2) Required platform contract: package/task CPU, memory, disk, process/time,
tool/data/network limits, common across compared solvers of the same task.
Missing or unverified limits belong to environment/runtime integration, not a
requirement to supply the experimental answer.
(3) Legitimate solver decisions WITHIN that contract: datasets/settings, seed
schedule, repetitions, step-size/rate grids, iteration allocation, diagnostics,
fit windows, uncertainty analyses and tolerances. These are intentionally chosen
and justified by the solver. Their freedom alone is NOT an ambiguity, scientific
defect, or reason to reject materials. Do not demand fixed repetitions, exact
iteration counts, universal grids or identical tolerances just for comparability.
A fixed method may require positive/constant steps or rank assumptions; specify
those semantics without preselecting all experimental values. Flag only an
actual contradiction, omitted defining condition or inability to construct a
valid informative CPU experiment under the package limits, and give evidence.
Material review is not a review of the as-yet-unwritten solver experiment.
Check EACH task's input/output contract and every public asset, target-answer or
cross-stage leakage, working starting code vs target implementation, background
coverage and earliest disclosure uncertainty. Titles removed is not no leakage.
Ensure WRITE source data is labelled aggregate/raw accurately and no invented CIs.
For WRITE_EVIDENCE, supplied authentic data, provenance and generic parsing
helpers are allowed. A public ready-made renderer that already chooses the
target plot, mapping, scale, layout and labels substantially performs the task;
flag this as over-scaffolding even if labelled optional and newly authored.
The solver should design and implement its own evidence presentation. Dependency
smoke may render unrelated synthetic data, but must not supply the target figure
or its answer-like generation program as task input. A numeric manifest given
for provenance is not itself proof of the solver's rendered output correctness.
Do not force every paper to support all task types; validate unsupported reasons.
Per-package Docker spec and limits must be justified and remain runtime-unverified
until the controller actually builds and smoke-tests the fresh container path.
Source license is not blanket permission for papers/data or derivative release.

A program's hash/shape pass does not validate source semantics, historical
completeness, safety, rights or judge behavior. Verify at least every core method,
hypothesis and numerical evidence record against originals. Explicitly enumerate
anything not actually checked. You cannot grant formal acceptance or rank models.

